From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maicon Alves <alvesmaiconn@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 02:49:43 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 11/13] client: merge simplified faces, and leave out far
 detail meshes

Equal faces next to each other in a simplified mesh (same node, param2
and light) become one quad when the texture tiles, and an opaque liquid
(translucent_liquids = false) hides the faces of solid cells. Lake view:
679,198 -> 529,246 vertices.

Detail meshes of blocks beyond client_lod_distance plus 32 nodes were
made and kept for nothing. Now a block received there gets no detail
mesh and is acked right away, since no mesh result would ack it; a far
block's detail mesh is dropped when the BFS culler visits it; and a
block left out is meshed again once its region comes within those 32
nodes, before it is drawn in detail. With the loops culler or range_all,
which don't draw simplified meshes, every block is meshed again.

Flying over the lake and back (300 nodes at 6 nodes/s), the client's
RSS on llvmpipe peaked at 571 MB instead of 708 MB.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

